## Ideal Answer (interview me bolo):

Main Hybrid approach use karunga — API Gateway par global per-user limit enforce hogi, aur har service apne endpoints ke liye 
service-specific limit enforce karegi. Matlab, ya to per-user per-service rate limit, ya phir per-user per-service per-endpoint 
limit us service ke andar. Isse centralized control bhi milega aur fine-grained flexibility bhi.


### NOTE:
----------

Modern API Gateways (Kong, AWS API Gateway, Spring Cloud Gateway) route ke basis par Per-Service, Per-User Rate Limiting support kar sakte hain.
Gateway URL pattern se service identify karta hai aur us user ki us service ke sabhi endpoints ki requests ko collectively count karta hai.

/api/users/**     (User Service)    → 5000 req/min per user (across all User Service endpoints)
/api/payments/**  (Payment Service) → 100 req/min per user (across all Payment Service endpoints)
/api/orders/**    (Order Service)   → 2000 req/min per user (across all Order Service endpoints)

Important: Ye Per-Service, Per-User rate limiting hai, Per-Endpoint rate limiting nahi.
Matlab ek service ke sabhi endpoints ka combined request count hota hai, har endpoint ka separate count nahi.



