Q5. Rules static rahenge ya dynamic?
---------------------------------------

Khudke samjh ke liye - 


1. STATIC CONFIGURATION
-------------------------

- Rate limit ke rules API Gateway / Service ke config. file me hardcoded (application.yml)
- Fayda: Simple, fast (koi DB call nahi)
- Nuksaan: 
  - Har change ke liye service restart karna padta hai → Downtime
  - Emergency me (jaise attack aa gaya aur turant limit tighten
    karni ho) possible nahi hai — pehle config file change karo,
    phir application/API Gateway restart karo — isme time lagta hai


2. DYNAMIC CONFIGURATION
-------------------------

- Rate limit ke rules DB me stored hote hain (jaise: per user 100 requests/min).
- Problem: Har request ko validate karne ke liye DB call → DB overload
- SOLUTION: LAYERED CACHE ARCHITECTURE

    Local Cache (Har instance ka apna)
         │
    Distributed Cache (Redis)
         │
    Database (Source of truth)



